  "analysis_notes": "Patch b56ab27 by Jeff King simplifies internals of dequoting in quote.c. Changes: (1) Inlines static sq_dequote_to_argv_internal() into the public sq_dequote_to_strvec(), removing the indirection layer. (2) Removes dead argv-branch code (ALLOC_GROW/*argv path) that was never reachable through the public API. (3) Removes conditional if(array) guard since array is always non-NULL via public signature. The public API sq_dequote_to_strvec(char *arg, struct strvec *array) declared in quote.h has identical signature and identical observable behavior for all existing callers (bisect.c, builtin/am.c, builtin/bisect.c). The removed sq_dequote_to_argv_internal was static (internal linkage). Both candidates in candidates.json have is_public: false and surface: []. This is a pure internal refactoring with zero compatibility impact."
